        "text": "Scanner input methods in Java",
        "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001", "Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004", "Q0005"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null,
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "The Scanner class provides several methods for reading different types of input: `nextByte()` reads a byte value, `nextInt()` reads an int, `nextFloat()`/`nextDouble()` read floating‑point numbers, `next()` reads the next token (delimited by whitespace), and `nextLine()` reads the remainder of the current line including the line‑separator. `next()` returns a token, so when a user enters a full name separated by a space, two calls to `next()` are needed to obtain both parts. `nextLine()` consumes the line‑separator that `print()` leaves, which is why output appears on the next line after a `print` call.",
        "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001", "Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004", "Q0005"]
      }
    }
  ],
  "examples": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "`nextByte()` returns a byte value that can be stored in a byte variable.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When concatenating a string with a byte, Java performs implicit casting of the byte to a string.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "`print()` does not add a newline after the output, while `println()` does.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If a floating‑point number (e.g., 20.1) is entered when `nextInt()` is expected, a `InputMismatchException` is thrown because the method can only parse integer values.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "`nextFloat()` or `nextDouble()` must be used to read floating‑point numbers.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "`next()` returns a token; each call reads up to the next whitespace delimiter.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When reading a full name with a space, two calls to `next()` are required to obtain both tokens.",
        "refs": ["Q0004", "Q0005"]
      }
    }
  ],
